      "post_id": "91451",
      "author_handle": "rose61",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 years 6 months ago",
      "body": "Babies are wonderful to have.Taking care of a baby can be wonderful until it starts crying and all efforts to calm them down delay to bear fruit.What are the best approaches to calming down a crying baby?",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10823/#91451",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/4b10292ad690bb03ce88.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10823/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "91451"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "91455",
      "author_handle": "neneth",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 years 6 months ago",
      "body": "Some babies cry more than others for reasons we don’t fully understand. This doesn’t mean that you are doing anything wrong as a parent or that your baby doesn’t like you! Many parents have to cope with babies who cry a lot in the early months of life. If you have found yourself bouncing, patting, humming, or soothing a fussy baby, you are not alone!",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10823/#91455",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/4b10292ad690bb03ce88.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10823/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "91451"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "93654",
      "author_handle": "Will_Lily",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 1 year 7 months ago",
      "body": "Juggling work and childcare as a single parent is tough but finding a nursery with longer hours can help. Moving closer to family or joining local groups might also make things easier.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10823/#93654",
